course: dictionary
lesson: 503
title: Medicine words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Aspirin is a medicine. It reduces pain, fever and swelling. Read the words around it to learn more: «Aspirin should not be given to children under 16 unless a doctor says so.» The clue words are doctor and under 16, so adults and doctors decide when medicine is given, not children.
explain: Aspirin can be a word for the medicine itself, as in «a packet of aspirin», or a word for one tablet, as in «take an aspirin». Check the words around it: a packet holds many tablets, but take an aspirin means one.
explain: «Medicine is chosen by adults and doctors.» Never take medicine on your own. Ask a parent, doctor or nurse, and always use the right amount. Context tells you what is safe, so read it carefully.
fact: Aspirin is a medicine that reduces pain, fever and swelling.
fact: An aspirin is one tablet of this medicine.
fact: Aspirin is usually not given to children under 16, because it can cause a rare but serious illness called Reye's syndrome.
fact: The first form of aspirin came from willow bark, which has a chemical that eases pain.
fact: Children are usually given other medicines, such as paracetamol, instead.
exercise: Who should decide whether a child under 16 is given aspirin? | A shop assistant | A friend at school | The child | *A doctor
exercise: «Aspirin is a medicine that reduces pain.» What does reduces mean? | Makes louder | Makes faster | Makes bigger | *Makes smaller
exercise: In «take an aspirin», how many tablets is that? | None | *One | A whole packet | Two
test: «Aspirin should not be given to children under 16, because it can cause a rare but serious illness.» What does rare mean here? | Very tasty | Very old | Very common | *Not common
test: Why are children usually given paracetamol instead of aspirin? | Aspirin tastes bad | Paracetamol is older than aspirin | Paracetamol is only for adults | *Aspirin can cause Reye's syndrome in children under 16
exam: Where did the first form of aspirin come from? | Oak trees | Sea water | *Willow bark | Ibuprofen tablets
